vkd3d: use existing GPU address realignment on KosmicKrisp

ReSkate logs a 64 KiB alignment request backed by a 16 KiB-aligned Metal GPU
address. The existing padded allocation path handles this for Turnip but
assumes other drivers satisfy 64 KiB alignment. Classify KosmicKrisp correctly.
Only allocations requesting aligned observable GPU addresses use padding; the
existing host-pointer, external-memory, scratch and feature exclusions remain.

Generated-by: LLM

